# Read docs before changing code

Before planning, implementing, or refactoring anything in this repo, read the relevant files under `docs/`:

| When working on… | Read first |
| --- | --- |
| Any structural or feature change | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| UI, styling, widgets, tokens | `docs/DESIGN.md` |
| Database, SQL, models, Supabase | `docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` |
| Auth0 login / callbacks | `docs/auth0_setup.md` |
| Supabase setup, RLS, migrations | `docs/supabase_setup.md` |

## Workflow

1. Identify which doc(s) apply to the task.
2. Read them (use the Read tool — do not guess from memory).
3. Align the change with conventions in those docs (layers, tokens, schema, RLS).
4. If the change contradicts a doc, update the doc in the same PR/session.

## Do not

- Hardcode colors, radii, or durations — follow `docs/DESIGN.md` and `lib/config/design_tokens.dart`.
- Add tables or columns without checking `docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` and `sql/`.
- Bypass `AuthService` / `requesting_user_id()` patterns documented in architecture and setup docs.

Entry index: root `README.md` links all docs.
